# ---------------------------------- Space-Tracker source-dataset indexes ----
# The internal layer's two manifests (463 SOT / 491 MOT sequences). They index
# the *source* datasets in their original on-disk formats and are needed only to
# rebuild the release; the released package ships its own manifests inside
# sot/ and mot/. Kept locally so the annotation tool and the build scripts run,
# never published — their sequence counts are not the benchmark's and having
# them in the tree invites readers to quote the wrong numbers.
space_tracker/space_tracker.json
space_tracker/space_tracker_mot.json

# ------------------------------------------------ internal working notes ----
# docs/ is the project's own lab notebook: dataset audits, split statistics,
# per-experiment findings and the review tool's decision log. None of it is
# needed to run the benchmark or to read the paper, and it is regenerated by
# the tools/ scripts. The four files the library actually loads at runtime
# live in space_tracker/data/ and space_tracker/splits.json; the figures the
# README embeds live in assets/.
docs/
